{"title":"Career Roadmap: Policy Researcher","role":"Policy Researcher","summary":"A Policy Researcher studies public problems, evaluates policies and programmes, analyzes economic and social data, and produces evidence that can support government, think tanks, NGOs, research institutions, international organizations and consulting firms.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Economics"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Develop economic analysis, research methodology, quantitative skills, policy evaluation and evidence-based policy communication"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Policy Researcher studies public problems, evaluates policies and programmes, analyzes economic and social data, and produces evidence that can support government, think tanks, NGOs, research institutions, international organizations and consulting firms."},{"type":"p","text":"The typical workflow is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy Problem","Research Question","Literature & Evidence","Data Collection","Analysis","Policy Evaluation","Findings","Recommendations","Policy Brief","Stakeholder Communication"]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, BA Economics provides a strong foundation in economic reasoning, statistics and public-policy analysis. However, a strong candidate should add econometrics, research methods, data analysis, public policy and policy writing."},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate will often begin as a Research Assistant, Policy Research Associate, Economic Research Assistant, Research Analyst or Programme Research Associate before progressing to Policy Researcher/Analyst roles."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Economics & research foundation"},{"text":"Microeconomics, macroeconomics, statistics"},{"text":"Research notes + basic analysis"},{"text":"Only theoretical economics"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Econometrics, data analysis, research methods"},{"text":"Data-analysis projects"},{"text":"Weak statistics"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Policy specialization"},{"text":"Public economics, development, governance"},{"text":"Policy briefs + evaluations"},{"text":"Writing without evidence"}],[{"text":"Year 4*"},{"text":"Advanced research"},{"text":"Policy analysis, advanced econometrics, internship"},{"text":"Dissertation + research portfolio"},{"text":"No practical research experience"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"*For a 4-year honours structure. In a 3-year BA, integrate the Year 4 objectives into the final year."}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1 — Economics Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microeconomics"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Basic mathematics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Economic history"},{"text":"Political institutions"},{"text":"Sociology fundamentals"},{"text":"Academic writing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economic news-reading habit"},{"text":"Basic data interpretation"},{"text":"Research-note system"},{"text":"Excel fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2 — Economic Systems & Public Issues"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Demand and supply"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Production"},{"text":"Market structures"},{"text":"National income"},{"text":"Inflation"},{"text":"Unemployment"},{"text":"Economic growth"},{"text":"Fiscal policy"},{"text":"Monetary policy"},{"text":"International trade"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Start connecting theory with real-world policy questions."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why is unemployment high?"},{"text":"What causes food-price inflation?"},{"text":"How does a subsidy affect consumers and producers?"},{"text":"What determines economic growth?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3 — Statistics & Econometrics"},{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most important stages for a policy researcher."},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Distributions"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Econometrics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Simple linear regression"},{"text":"Multiple regression"},{"text":"OLS"},{"text":"Dummy variables"},{"text":"Interaction terms"},{"text":"Multicollinearity"},{"text":"Heteroskedasticity"},{"text":"Autocorrelation"},{"text":"Model specification"},{"text":"Statistical significance"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Causality vs correlation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The key principle:"},{"type":"p","text":"Correlation does not automatically establish causation."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4 — Public Economics & Policy"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Economics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public goods"},{"text":"Externalities"},{"text":"Taxation"},{"text":"Subsidies"},{"text":"Redistribution"},{"text":"Welfare economics"},{"text":"Market failure"},{"text":"Government intervention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Development Economics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Poverty"},{"text":"Inequality"},{"text":"Human capital"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Employment"},{"text":"Productivity"},{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"Financial inclusion"},{"text":"Rural development"},{"text":"Gender and development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Public Policy"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem Identification","Policy Design","Implementation","Monitoring","Evaluation","Revision"]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stakeholders"},{"text":"Policy objectives"},{"text":"Alternatives"},{"text":"Costs"},{"text":"Benefits"},{"text":"Risks"},{"text":"Implementation capacity"},{"text":"Unintended consequences"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5 — Research Methods & Policy Evaluation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to conduct professional policy research."},{"type":"h","text":"Research Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research questions"},{"text":"Hypotheses"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Conceptual frameworks"},{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Primary research"},{"text":"Secondary research"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Mixed-method research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Policy Evaluation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Baseline"},{"text":"Treatment/intervention"},{"text":"Control/comparison groups"},{"text":"Outcome indicators"},{"text":"Impact evaluation"},{"text":"Cost-benefit analysis"},{"text":"Cost-effectiveness analysis"},{"text":"Monitoring & evaluation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Where appropriate, understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Randomized controlled trials"},{"text":"Difference-in-differences"},{"text":"Regression discontinuity"},{"text":"Instrumental variables"},{"text":"Matching"},{"text":"Panel-data methods"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Students do not need to master every advanced causal method during undergraduate study, but should understand their logic and limitations."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 6 — Policy Research Specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one or two areas."},{"type":"table","header":["Specialization","Possible Research Areas"],"rows":[[{"text":"Economic Policy"},{"text":"Inflation, taxation, fiscal policy"}],[{"text":"Labour Policy"},{"text":"Employment, wages, skills"}],[{"text":"Education Policy"},{"text":"Access, quality, learning outcomes"}],[{"text":"Health Policy"},{"text":"Healthcare access, insurance, outcomes"}],[{"text":"Agriculture Policy"},{"text":"Farm income, markets, subsidies"}],[{"text":"Social Policy"},{"text":"Poverty, welfare, inequality"}],[{"text":"Environmental Policy"},{"text":"Climate, pollution, sustainability"}],[{"text":"Urban Policy"},{"text":"Housing, transport, infrastructure"}],[{"text":"Rural Development"},{"text":"Rural livelihoods, public services"}],[{"text":"Financial Policy"},{"text":"Banking, inclusion, regulation"}],[{"text":"Technology Policy"},{"text":"AI, digital economy, data governance"}],[{"text":"Trade Policy"},{"text":"Imports, exports, global trade"}],[{"text":"International Development"},{"text":"Development finance and global institutions"}]]}]},{"heading":"Economic Policy Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A policy researcher should be able to analyze:"},{"type":"h","text":"Fiscal Policy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government revenue"},{"text":"Government expenditure"},{"text":"Fiscal deficit"},{"text":"Public debt"},{"text":"Taxation"},{"text":"Subsidies"},{"text":"Public investment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Monetary Policy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Inflation"},{"text":"Interest rates"},{"text":"Money supply"},{"text":"Credit"},{"text":"Monetary transmission"},{"text":"Central-bank policy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Labour Economics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Employment"},{"text":"Unemployment"},{"text":"Labour-force participation"},{"text":"Wages"},{"text":"Informal employment"},{"text":"Skills"},{"text":"Productivity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Development"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Poverty"},{"text":"Inequality"},{"text":"Human development"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"Productivity"}]}]},{"heading":"Policy Research Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional research project should follow:"},{"type":"h","text":"Step 1 — Identify the Problem"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Youth unemployment remains high despite increasing educational attainment."},{"type":"h","text":"Step 2 — Define the Research Question"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Which factors are associated with youth unemployment among graduates?"},{"type":"h","text":"Step 3 — Review Existing Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic papers"},{"text":"Government reports"},{"text":"Official statistics"},{"text":"International datasets"},{"text":"Previous evaluations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 4 — Collect Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential sources:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government datasets"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Administrative data"},{"text":"International databases"},{"text":"Research datasets"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 5 — Analyze"},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Trend analysis"},{"text":"Segmentation"},{"text":"Comparative analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 6 — Interpret"},{"type":"p","text":"Ask:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What does the evidence show?"},{"text":"What does it not show?"},{"text":"What are the limitations?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 7 — Recommend"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop realistic policy alternatives."},{"type":"h","text":"Step 8 — Communicate"},{"type":"p","text":"Produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research report"},{"text":"Policy brief"},{"text":"Executive summary"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Data visualization"}]}]},{"heading":"Data & Quantitative Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"IF"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"COUNTIFS"},{"text":"PivotTables"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Scenario analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical Software"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn at least one:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Stata"},{"text":"SPSS"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For economics/policy research, R or Stata can be particularly useful, while Python provides broader data-science applications."},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful libraries:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"seaborn"},{"text":"statsmodels"},{"text":"scikit-learn"}]},{"type":"h","text":"SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"CASE"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"SQL becomes useful when policy datasets are stored in relational databases."}]},{"heading":"Data Visualization","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to communicate research findings visually."},{"type":"p","text":"Tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Tableau"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"GIS/QGIS"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trend charts"},{"text":"Geographic maps"},{"text":"Poverty dashboards"},{"text":"Employment dashboards"},{"text":"Education indicators"},{"text":"Health indicators"},{"text":"Government expenditure dashboards"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A good policy visualization should make the evidence easier to understand, not simply make the report visually attractive."}]},{"heading":"Research Writing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Policy Researcher should be able to produce:"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Paper"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Abstract"},{"text":"Introduction"},{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Methodology"},{"text":"Data"},{"text":"Results"},{"text":"Discussion"},{"text":"Limitations"},{"text":"Conclusion"},{"text":"References"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Policy Brief"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Executive summary"},{"text":"Problem"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Current policy"},{"text":"Policy gaps"},{"text":"Options"},{"text":"Recommendation"},{"text":"Implementation"},{"text":"Risks"},{"text":"References"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice writing in a concise, evidence-based style."}]},{"heading":"Critical Thinking & Evidence Evaluation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to distinguish:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fact vs opinion"},{"text":"Correlation vs causation"},{"text":"Association vs impact"},{"text":"Evidence vs anecdote"},{"text":"Primary vs secondary sources"},{"text":"Peer-reviewed research vs commentary"},{"text":"Statistical significance vs practical significance"},{"text":"Short-term vs long-term effects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Selection bias"},{"text":"Measurement bias"},{"text":"Sampling bias"},{"text":"Confounding"},{"text":"Data-quality problems"},{"text":"Missing data"},{"text":"Publication bias"}]}]},{"heading":"Government & Governance Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For India-focused policy research, understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Constitution"},{"text":"Parliament"},{"text":"Union government"},{"text":"State governments"},{"text":"Local governments"},{"text":"Ministries and departments"},{"text":"Regulatory institutions"},{"text":"Public finance"},{"text":"Government schemes"},{"text":"Public-sector programmes"},{"text":"Decentralization"},{"text":"E-governance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Study how a policy moves from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Legislation/Policy","Budget","Programme Design","Implementation","Monitoring","Evaluation"]}]},{"heading":"Policy Evaluation Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Government Scheme Evaluation"},{"type":"p","text":"Select a public programme."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Objective"},{"text":"Target population"},{"text":"Budget"},{"text":"Eligibility"},{"text":"Implementation mechanism"},{"text":"Coverage"},{"text":"Outcomes"},{"text":"Challenges"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Recommendations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce a 10–15 page policy evaluation report."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Employment Policy Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Study employment trends using publicly available data."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Labour-force participation"},{"text":"Employment"},{"text":"Unemployment"},{"text":"Gender differences"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Urban/rural differences"},{"text":"Youth employment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dataset"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Power BI dashboard"},{"text":"Policy brief"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Inflation & Household Welfare"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Inflation trends"},{"text":"Food inflation"},{"text":"Fuel prices"},{"text":"Household expenditure"},{"text":"Income effects"},{"text":"Policy responses"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce an evidence-based policy report."}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Economic Policy Intelligence & Evaluation Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a research platform that combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Public Data","Cleaning","Statistical Analysis","Policy Evaluation","Visualization","Policy Recommendation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economic indicators"},{"text":"Employment data"},{"text":"Inflation"},{"text":"Poverty/inequality indicators"},{"text":"Government expenditure"},{"text":"State/district comparisons"},{"text":"Time-series analysis"},{"text":"Regression analysis"},{"text":"Policy evaluation"},{"text":"Power BI dashboard"},{"text":"Automated research reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final deliverables"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research paper"},{"text":"Policy brief"},{"text":"Dataset"},{"text":"Econometric analysis"},{"text":"Dashboard"},{"text":"Visualizations"},{"text":"Methodology documentation"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Policy recommendations"}]}]},{"heading":"Research Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"R / Stata / Python"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Word/Google Docs"},{"text":"Reference-management software"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Tableau"},{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research & Reference"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic databases"},{"text":"Government statistical portals"},{"text":"Research repositories"},{"text":"Institutional reports"},{"text":"Survey datasets"},{"text":"Economic databases"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Always record the source, methodology, date and definition of indicators when using data."}]},{"heading":"AI for Policy Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI can support research but should not replace evidence verification."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature discovery"},{"text":"Research summarization"},{"text":"Data-cleaning assistance"},{"text":"Coding assistance"},{"text":"Data exploration"},{"text":"Document comparison"},{"text":"Policy-document analysis"},{"text":"Classification"},{"text":"Information extraction"},{"text":"Visualization assistance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy Documents","AI-assisted extraction","Human verification","Structured database","Analysis"]},{"type":"p","text":"Important risks:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hallucinated sources"},{"text":"Fabricated statistics"},{"text":"Incorrect interpretation"},{"text":"Bias"},{"text":"Privacy concerns"},{"text":"Reproducibility problems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For serious research, every important claim should be traceable to the original source."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"Government research bodies"},{"text":"Public-policy organizations"},{"text":"Economic research institutions"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Development organizations"},{"text":"Consulting firms"},{"text":"Public-affairs firms"},{"text":"International development organizations"},{"text":"Financial/economic research teams"},{"text":"Research departments of large organizations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Ideal internship responsibilities:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Survey research"},{"text":"Policy research"},{"text":"Programme evaluation"},{"text":"Report writing"},{"text":"Policy brief preparation"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful supplementary areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Econometrics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Development economics"},{"text":"Data analytics"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"Stata"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Monitoring & evaluation"},{"text":"Impact evaluation"},{"text":"Public finance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, research output and quantitative competence generally matter more than accumulating many certificates."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After graduation, realistic roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Policy Research Assistant"},{"text":"Policy Research Associate"},{"text":"Research Analyst"},{"text":"Economic Research Assistant"},{"text":"Economic Research Analyst"},{"text":"Public Policy Associate"},{"text":"Policy Analyst Trainee"},{"text":"Programme Research Associate"},{"text":"Development Research Associate"},{"text":"Monitoring & Evaluation Associate"},{"text":"Social Impact Analyst"},{"text":"Data Research Analyst"},{"text":"Public Affairs Research Associate"},{"text":"Legislative Research Associate"},{"text":"Think Tank Research Associate"},{"text":"Junior Economist*"}]},{"type":"p","text":"*Economist titles and responsibilities can have stronger academic/quantitative requirements depending on the employer."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For long-term policy research, postgraduate study can be highly valuable."},{"type":"h","text":"Economics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Economics"},{"text":"MSc Economics"},{"text":"Applied Economics"},{"text":"Econometrics"},{"text":"Development Economics"},{"text":"Financial Economics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Public Policy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Master's in Public Policy"},{"text":"Public Administration"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Development Studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative Fields"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Data Science"},{"text":"Econometrics"},{"text":"Applied Statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"International Relations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"International Development"},{"text":"Political Economy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong postgraduate programme can substantially deepen econometrics, causal inference, research design and policy evaluation."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate fields include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Economics"},{"text":"MSc Applied Economics"},{"text":"MSc Econometrics"},{"text":"MSc Development Economics"},{"text":"Master of Public Policy"},{"text":"Master of Public Administration"},{"text":"MSc Public Policy"},{"text":"MSc Public Economics"},{"text":"MSc International Development"},{"text":"MSc Political Economy"},{"text":"MSc Data Science for Public Policy"},{"text":"Social Data Science"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For quantitative programmes, verify prerequisites in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Econometrics"},{"text":"Programming"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Policy Research Track"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Policy Researcher / Policy Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Researcher / Senior Policy Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Lead / Programme Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Director / Policy Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Director / Senior Policy Leadership"},{"type":"h","text":"Economics Track"},{"type":"h","text":"Economic Research Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Economic Research Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Economist / Senior Economist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Economist / Research Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Economic Research Director"},{"type":"p","text":"Progression varies significantly between think tanks, government institutions, consulting firms, universities and international organizations."}]},{"heading":"Long-Term Relevance: 2030–2046","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Future policy research will increasingly combine economics with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI policy"},{"text":"Digital public infrastructure"},{"text":"Climate economics"},{"text":"Energy transition"},{"text":"Health economics"},{"text":"Education analytics"},{"text":"Labour-market analytics"},{"text":"Geospatial analysis"},{"text":"Real-time economic indicators"},{"text":"Computational social science"},{"text":"Public-sector data science"},{"text":"AI governance"},{"text":"Digital regulation"},{"text":"Data privacy"},{"text":"Algorithmic accountability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future profile is likely to be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Economics","Econometrics","Policy","Data","Technology","Research Communication"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Economics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microeconomics"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Public economics"},{"text":"Development economics"},{"text":"Labour economics"},{"text":"International economics"},{"text":"Environmental economics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Econometrics"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Causal inference fundamentals"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Research methodology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"R/Stata/Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"GIS basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Policy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy analysis"},{"text":"Policy evaluation"},{"text":"Public finance"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Programme implementation"},{"text":"Monitoring & evaluation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Policy briefs"},{"text":"Evidence evaluation"},{"text":"Citation and research ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Critical thinking"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Stakeholder management"},{"text":"Project management"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Portfolio Target","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong economics foundation"},{"text":"Statistics and econometrics competence"},{"text":"At least one statistical programming language — R/Stata/Python"},{"text":"Excel proficiency"},{"text":"SQL fundamentals"},{"text":"Power BI/data visualization"},{"text":"Three policy research projects"},{"text":"One government-scheme evaluation"},{"text":"One econometric research project"},{"text":"One policy brief"},{"text":"One substantial research paper/dissertation"},{"text":"One policy dashboard"},{"text":"Research internship"},{"text":"Literature-review portfolio"},{"text":"AI-assisted research workflow with source verification"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Graduate Profile"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Economics","Microeconomics","Macroeconomics","Statistics","Econometrics","Research Methods","Public Economics","Development Economics","Governance","Policy Analysis","Data Analysis","Policy Evaluation","Causal Inference","R/Stata/Python","Excel/SQL","Data Visualization","Policy Writing","Internship","Research Assistant/Policy Research Associate","Policy Researcher/Analyst","Senior Researcher","Research/Policy Lead","Research Director/Policy Director"]},{"type":"table","header":["1414","UG","Humanities & Social Sciences","BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Economics","Financial Analyst","—"],"rows":[]}]}]}